    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0446" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1197/732: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-26T15:00:00-04:00">May 26, 1934—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. For Fuller. American Embassy at London states that it has mailed to you a
                    copy of its telegram No. 276, dated May 25, 3 p.m., to the Department<anchor
                        n="12" xml:id="d258-f1"/> reporting that British Government has decided that
                    no action is at the moment necessary in regard to the League’s communication
                    requesting information on narcotic traffic in Manchuria.</p>
                <p>The Department will, pending your return, hold in abeyance the question of
                    replying to the League’s communication under reference unless, in the light of
                    information available to you, further consideration of the matter appears
                    advisable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
